* refactor(pools): use scoped rayon pools

* Avoid starting a pool for an empty queue

* Avoid an unused import on overlayfs

* fix(pools): guard the forking parent and bound pool width

* Keep one execution path and mark daemon on entry

* fix(pools): retry deferred trash and size fixed batches

* Avoid overlayfs-only unused variant warning

* Gate dynamic pool support where used

* fix(service): retry trash through locked background emptiers

* Merge origin/main and preserve shared APFS threshold

* Restore worker count helper used by chunked transfers

* fix(apfs): require Send for parallel callback
5c2670db0da16920f94a0e59792721b9bc67e310feat(review): change diff --since-review --person <login> starts at that person's approval (#342)

A person approves through a signed request, with the person as signer, so the machine
and uid rule of --since-review never found it. With --person the diff starts at the
newest version that person approved (an approval not withdrawn, with a pinned key).


